alyssa: Heads-up: opened PR to update err-ref and docs for 429s observed when high-cardinality context windows hit timeouts. Looking for quick review + SDK snippet for trimming + backoff. PR: https://github.com/redwood/docs/pull/1234

mike: Saw the repro in staging — high token count + concurrent streams. Logs show '429: too many requests' correlated with per-shard queue length. Minimal reproducer: ```bash curl -X POST /v1/generate -d '{"prompt":"a"*15000,"stream":true}'```

joan: Thanks — can we clarify fallback text: recommend passive fallback to lower-context variant (pin shorter model) + 429 backoff with exponential jitter. Short copy suggestion: 'On 429s from capacity surge, automatically retry with exponential backoff up to 3 attempts; if still failing, issue fallback request with trimmed context (remove oldest messages) or use a lower-seq-length model.'

mike: Agree. Also add note about batching: if user enables large batching windows we should call out increased latency-to-429 tradeoff. I'll add small diag image to PR.

doc-bot: CI: docs lint OK, link-check failed for internal-model-naming.md -> 404. @alyssa can you confirm path? :link: 

alyssa: Ack. I'll fix link to /models/variants.md and push. Also adding SDK snippet for JS to show context trimming + retry: ```js
// pseudo
async function generateWithTrim(promptList){
  let attempt=0;
  while(attempt<3){
    try{
      return await client.generate({prompt:promptList.join(' ')});
    }catch(e){
      if(e.status===429){
        await sleep(200 * Math.pow(2,attempt));
        trimOldest(promptList);
        attempt++;
        continue;
      }
      throw e;
    }
  }
  // final fallback: call lower-seq model
  return await client.generate({model:'redwood-medium', prompt:trimToWindow(promptList,4096)});
}
```

sasha: LGTM. One ask: include telemetry tag example so ops can filter these fallback events (errref: timeout.cardinality.fallback=true).

alyssa: Will add. Plan: patch link, add SDK snippet, include short dev-facing note about 'cardinality' term (what we mean by it). Target merge EOD. @joan want to review text before merge?

joan: I'll do a quick pass this afternoon. :+1:
